# In a dyadic train each tine takes both arguments; r_ev takes one,
# and the note says so.
== SOURCE
1 2 [r_ev + a_bs] 3 4
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected a number, found a -> b
 --> -e:1:6
  |
1 | 1 2 [r_ev + a_bs] 3 4
  |      ^^^^
  = note: `r_ev` has type a -> a
  = note: in the train `[r_ev + a_bs]`, `r_ev` is applied as `x r_ev y`, where x and y are the train's arguments
  = note: `r_ev` takes one argument, but here it is given two
